  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00001",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[1]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 1,
      "endIndex": 186,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "The Wintermute Alpha Challenge is a set of investigations into how blockchain systems behave when contracts, transaction history, market structure, and cross-chain infrastructure meet.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00002",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[2]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 186,
      "endIndex": 519,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "The cases ask very different things of the solver: finding an address from onchain evidence, resolving a dispute game, reconstructing a historical auction, or reaching an L2 that does not expose a conventional bridge. What connects them is the need to reason from first principles rather than treating the blockchain as a black box.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00003",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[3]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 519,
      "endIndex": 815,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "This article documents the reasoning behind each solution. It is not intended as an answer key or a collection of opaque scripts. Every case starts with the relevant concepts, then explains how to identify the useful evidence, how to test a hypothesis, and finally how to reproduce the solution.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00004",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[4]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 815,
      "endIndex": 991,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "The objective is not only to show what works, but to explain why it works, which assumptions make it valid, and how the same reasoning can be applied to a new onchain problem.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00005",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[5]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 991,
      "endIndex": 1018,
      "namedStyleType": "HEADING_2",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "## Case 01: Out of Nowhere",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00006",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[6]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 1018,
      "endIndex": 1311,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "The case begins with a large [USDC transfer](https://etherscan.io/tx/0xe7b8d46c3f3e5f727cb42c9dfe7fc36855ab5092cf160e4c8812a2a27a84350b) on Ethereum. Roughly $1.5 million is sent from Allbridge to an address that provides bridge liquidity. Looking only at Ethereum, the transfer appears to come out of nowhere. The task is to identify the transaction on the source chain that caused it.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00007",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[7]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 1311,
      "endIndex": 1312,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00008",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[8]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 1312,
      "endIndex": 1418,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "A useful first lesson is that a bridge transfer is a coordinated pair of actions on separate blockchains.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00009",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[9]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 1418,
      "endIndex": 1419,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00010",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[10]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 1419,
      "endIndex": 1421,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "[INLINE_OBJECT kix.h7bke2rjx1em]",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00011",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[11]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 1421,
      "endIndex": 1422,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00012",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[12]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 1422,
      "endIndex": 1621,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "The destination transaction proves that a release happened on Ethereum but it does not identify which source-chain initiated the transfer. To do that reliably, we need the bridge's correlation data.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00013",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[13]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 1621,
      "endIndex": 1926,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "The ERC-20 transfer shows Allbridge sending USDC to the recipient, but amounts and recipients are weak search keys. The same address can bridge repeatedly, and many transfers can have the same rounded value. The more useful evidence is in Allbridge's `Received` event in the Ethereum transaction receipt:",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00014",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[14]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 1926,
      "endIndex": 1928,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "[INLINE_OBJECT kix.abpyz2kdgcrt]",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00015",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[15]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 1928,
      "endIndex": 1970,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "The event tells us four different things:",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
